{
 "_comment": "Sounds (v0.63.0; game/sound.py). events: a game event -> a sound file in data/sounds/ (no .wav), or several (one is picked at random each time), with an optional volume (0-1, on top of the player's settings). steps: map symbol -> footstep kind (step_<kind> in events). ambience: where the Hunter is -> a looping sound (title: the title screen; city: Bytorsskug's streets; interior: inside any other building; hall: the guild hall; brisering; and each land out in the miasma, with _dark variants for dark places (v0.93.0; was _night)). music: where -> a file in data/music/ (no extension: name.ogg, else name.wav), the user's; for now the assistant's attempts from tools/sound/make_music.py and tools/sound/pieces.py (v0.102.0: Bytorsskug through the city, its buildings and the guild hall, one piece that carries on as you go in and out; v0.103.0: the title screen, the Brisering, and four for the miasma). stingers (v0.103.0): a big card -> a short piece in data/sounds/, on the music volume (begin, complete, out, faint, fallen, rank, chapter). Keys for music are the same as ambience. To swap a sound, put an OGG or WAV in data/sounds/ and point the event at it. The sounds themselves are made by tools/sound/make_sounds.py (placeholders).",
